  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1817.09 Appeal",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1817.09 Appeal. An applicant or license holder aggrieved by a department decision made pursuant to Env-A 1817.07, to deny an application, or Env-A 1817.08, to revoke a license, who wishes to appeal the decision shall appeal to the air resources council, within 30 days of the department’s decision, in accordance with RSA 21-O:14 and the rules adopted by the council, Ec-Air 200.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1, Revision Note #2, and Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Env-A 1800) #14104, eff 11-1-24, EXPIRES: 11-1-34",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1800.html"
